M5Stack Tab5 ESP32-P4 + C6 SDIO Linux  (NOMMU, BusyBox)

Account m5.  Its password is password= in /tmp/credentials.txt (read it as
root on the serial console); the first boot also prints it once as
ES_CREDENTIALS.  The Tab5 has no USB drive, so there is no credentials.txt to
edit and no autorun.  su asks for root_password= from the same file.

Commands
  files    ls cp mv rm mkdir find xargs stat tree du df tar gzip unzip
  text     cat less head tail grep sed awk cut sort uniq wc tr diff vi
  system   ps top free uptime dmesg kill pkill pgrep watch timeout lsmod
  network  ifconfig ip ping nslookup traceroute netstat nc wget arp
  users    id whoami who w last su passwd
  other    python3 (MicroPython)  hexdump xxd md5sum sha256sum date bc

Full list: busybox --list ; busybox-tools --list
